   "date": "2017-01-05T14:37:20Z",
   "subject": "How to reduce overlap between branches of an unrooted tree.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi!<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m plotting an unrooted tree with the following command</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">layout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;unrooted&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">  geom_tippoint</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></div></code></div>but, as you can see, the  terminal branches of the tree overlap extensively, which makes difficult to identify how many individuals belong to each clade.<br><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YFmpNSk9Xb8/WG5WrsvRItI/AAAAAAAAAHs/WDXCvrQddcYSDtxoGQUTcprLgX9nJZafACLcB/s1600/ggtree.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YFmpNSk9Xb8/WG5WrsvRItI/AAAAAAAAAHs/WDXCvrQddcYSDtxoGQUTcprLgX9nJZafACLcB/s1600/ggtree.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482819026000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hFtkvZeMO9X5_YSZgm9Q5\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YFmpNSk9Xb8/WG5WrsvRItI/AAAAAAAAAHs/WDXCvrQddcYSDtxoGQUTcprLgX9nJZafACLcB/s320/ggtree.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\"></a></p><div>A rendition of the same tree with standard plot produces a better results:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;unrooted&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">show</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tip</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font></div></code></div></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XD0w5My170g/WG5XRZqFSqI/AAAAAAAAAHw/pCHc7dmQfcYVhYL1sGPDM4SFTmySzrQuQCLcB/s1600/ape765.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XD0w5My170g/WG5XRZqFSqI/AAAAAAAAAHw/pCHc7dmQfcYVhYL1sGPDM4SFTmySzrQuQCLcB/s1600/ape765.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482819026000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tdduv8qGy5OnarMV-mIUr\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XD0w5My170g/WG5XRZqFSqI/AAAAAAAAAHw/pCHc7dmQfcYVhYL1sGPDM4SFTmySzrQuQCLcB/s320/ape765.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"> It would be perfect if I could emulate this branch distribution. So, how can I tell ggtree to produce more even spaces between branches?</p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "yIiID-CQFQAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
